menu "Vision pipeline"

    config VISION_SEED_DETECT_MIN_PERMILLE
        int "Seed for the detector confidence floor (per mille)"
        default 350
        range 1 999
        help
            Seeds NVS key vision/detect_min, which the kiosk reads only while
            the running models image is format 1. A format 2 image carries the
            threshold of its own detector, from ml/configs/common/quant.yaml
            (KEHOACH 6.2.2), and SET_CONFIG never changes it.

    config VISION_SEED_LIVE_MIN_PERMILLE
        int "Seed for the liveness floor (per mille)"
        default 500
        range 1 999
        help
            Seeds NVS key vision/live_min, read only for a format 1 models
            image, the way the detector seed is (KEHOACH 6.2.2).

    config VISION_SEED_MATCH_MIN_PERMILLE
        int "Seed for the cosine match floor (per mille)"
        default 450
        range 1 999
        help
            Seeds NVS key vision/match_min, read only for a format 1 models
            image, the way the detector seed is. Cosine of unit embeddings, so
            450 means 0.45 (KEHOACH 6.2.2).

    config VISION_SEED_FACE_MIN_PX
        int "Seed for the smallest face the pipeline verifies (frame pixels)"
        default 100
        range 16 480
        help
            Recognition warps the face onto 113x113. Someone standing at the
            distance the guide frame invites measures 107-110 px, so 113 was a
            gate nobody could clear from there (KEHOACH 2.1).

    config VISION_SEED_GUIDE_MIN_PERCENT
        int "Seed for the share of a face that must sit inside the guide (percent)"
        default 50
        range 1 100
        help
            Written to NVS key vision/guide_min on the first boot only. Half
            the face box inside the drawn guide lets someone standing a head
            off centre check in, and a face that is not on the glass is never
            judged, since the guide lies inside the preview slice (KEHOACH 4.5.5d).

    config VISION_SEED_PRESENT_MM
        int "Seed for the distance that counts as someone standing there (mm)"
        default 700
        range 40 1300
        help
            Written to NVS key vision/present_mm on the first boot only.
            Recognition works between 250 and 420 mm (KEHOACH 3), so the
            gate sits past that: someone inside this distance wakes the
            pipeline, which then asks them to come closer (KEHOACH 2.3D).

endmenu
